  "forecast_notes": [
    "2027–2029 is a conditional three-year design-in and share-gain window, not contracted backlog; orders usually 2–8 weeks per S7. 2030–2033 fades growth and margins; perpetuity 2034. Same WACC and terminal growth for all cases.",
    "Base 2027 gross margin 42%, RD 21%, selling/admin 7.5%, levies/impairment/FX 1.5% => EBIT 12%; 2029 44%/20.5%/7.5%/1.5% =>14.5%. All R&D and share pay remain expenses. PPA amortization stays in EBIT, added in DA only for FCFF, no artificial adjusted EPS.",
    "DA includes acquired finite-life PPA amortization. Recurring R&D and renewals expensed in EBIT; economic capex covers purchased software, equipment, new leases and known 0.2 acquisition, without double counting expensed R&D. DA fades rather than perpetual one-off PPA tax shield.",
    "Terminal reinvestment g/ROIC used, no permanent reliance on low cash capex or PPA DA. Base terminal ROIC 15% requires design IP/client retention and RD productivity; not observed current ROIC.",
    "Normalized tax 15% replaces current negative income-tax expense and temporary subsidiary holiday; a modeling allowance for permanent R&D deductions is not assumed. WACC 10.5% is judgment, illustrative 95% equity cost 10.9% + 5% after-tax debt cost 2.9% =10.5%, not measured CAPM.",
    "Revenue growth consumes 30% incremental NWC in base/bull, 35% in bear; no free revenue growth in reverse DCF, where capex scales with revenue and DA stays fixed because acquired finite-life PPA amortization dominates the near-term schedule.",
    "All associates excluded from bridge and earnings; no invented consensus, no revenue valuation premium for sampling/AVL inclusion. Pending acquisition closes only conditionally within Q4 cash budget."
